Chewedfeed for Android — the Chewedfeed dashboard on the Even Realities G1 under the ScouterKit firmware,
without a laptop. Copyright the ScouterKit authors. GPL-3.0-or-later (LICENSE): it reuses the Android glue of
examples/ssh, which is GPL.

It includes:
- ScouterKit's C++ library (scouter_kit/src): MIT (scouter_kit/LICENSE), with
  - Departure Mono 1.500 (https://github.com/rektdeckard/departure-mono), built in as
    src/base/departure_mono.inc: SIL Open Font License 1.1 (licenses/departure_mono/,
    scouter_kit/third_party/departure_mono);
  - moodycamel ConcurrentQueue 1.0.5 (https://github.com/cameron314/concurrentqueue): Simplified BSD
    (licenses/concurrentqueue/, scouter_kit/third_party/concurrentqueue);
  - TinyCrypt 0.2.8's SHA-256 (https://github.com/intel/tinycrypt): BSD-3-Clause (licenses/tinycrypt/,
    scouter_kit/third_party/tinycrypt).
The app's licenses/ folder is copied from scouter_kit/third_party at build time.

The source tree also has the Gradle 8.10.2 wrapper (gradlew, gradlew.bat, gradle/wrapper/; https://gradle.org):
Apache-2.0, as gradlew's header says. It is a build tool, not part of the app.
